{:id :EACL-FORMAL-021
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :manual-review
 :seed-or-trace
 "datomic/make-client/cache/subproblem-cache-config-forwarding"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :availability
 :affected-versions
 ["PR 101 worktree before Datomic subproblem-cache option forwarding"]
 :affected-backends [:datomic]
 :root-cause
 "Datomic's cache normalizer omitted the shared cache-capacity options and constructed the completed-artifact stores with defaults. DataScript and Datahike forwarded the same portable capacity settings. Datomic therefore rejected intended denotation/answer capacities and always installed the defaults."
 :fix
 "The Datomic cache boundary now forwards the flat count-capacity options into the shared cache constructor and relies on that constructor to validate every bound before the client is returned."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.datomic.config-test/flat-denotation-cache-config-is-forwarded-and-validated-test"
  "formal mutation :datomic-subproblem-config-dropped"]}
